      "title": "Compare declaration with execution",
      "eyebrow": "Learn",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Use this exact approved provider declaration:\n\n```hcl\nterraform {\n  required_providers {\n    aws = {\n      source = \"hashicorp/aws\"\n      version = \"= 6.0.0\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```",
          "role": "syntax",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.define_an_ec2_instance_with_terraform_hcl_and_a_pinned_provider"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.define_an_ec2_instance_with_terraform_hcl_and_a_pinned_provider#tb2",
              "aws_devops.define_an_ec2_instance_with_terraform_hcl_and_a_pinned_provider#tb4"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.define_an_ec2_instance_with_terraform_hcl_and_a_pinned_provider#f1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Compare the exact provider pin and resource settings against the supplied specification, then compare the inspected plan with those same values before the approved apply step. Keep provider selection, declaration, plan and verified instance settings separate in the evidence. The native EC2 foundation comes before interpreting these settings.",
          "role": "example",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.define_an_ec2_instance_with_terraform_hcl_and_a_pinned_provider"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.define_an_ec2_instance_with_terraform_hcl_and_a_pinned_provider#tb4"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.define_an_ec2_instance_with_terraform_hcl_and_a_pinned_provider#f1",
              "aws_devops.define_an_ec2_instance_with_terraform_hcl_and_a_pinned_provider#f2",
              "aws_devops.define_an_ec2_instance_with_terraform_hcl_and_a_pinned_provider#f3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "A plausible declaration and provider pin are not execution evidence. Initialization installs providers; planning inspects intended changes; the approved apply creates the instance. Completion still needs verification of the resulting instance settings, not just a matching declaration. Use the supplied version and bounded resource settings rather than designing different infrastructure.",
          "role": "misconception",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.define_an_ec2_instance_with_terraform_hcl_and_a_pinned_provider"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
